🟢 Level 1: Basic Indexing Practice
Use:
text = "Programming"
Print the first character.
Print the last character using negative indexing.
Print the 4th character.
Print the second last character.
Take input from user and print only the last character.

🟡 Level 2: Basic Slicing (Start : End)
Use:
word = "PythonDeveloper"
Print "Python" using slicing.
Print "Developer" using slicing.
Print "thon".
Print first 5 characters using slicing shortcut.
Print last 4 characters using negative slicing.

🟠 Level 3: Step Slicing (Important)
Use:
data = "ABCDEFGHIJK"
Print every second character.
Print every third character.
Print characters from index 1 to 8 with step 2.
Print entire string using slicing only.
Print the string in reverse order.

🔵 Level 4: Reverse Logic Thinking
Use:
text = "LearningPython"
Print  "Python"  using negative slicing only.
Print "gninraeL" using slicing.
Print "nohtyP" using slicing.
Print characters from index 10 to 4 in reverse order.
Without using [::-1], print the entire string in reverse.

🔥 Bonus Thinking Questions (Very Important)
Use:
sentence = "Today is Day-10"
Print "Day-10" using slicing.
Print "Today" in reverse using slicing only.
Print "is" using slicing.
Print every second character from entire sentence.
Predict the output before running: print(sentence[-1:-6:-1])
